opendrop-rs for Debian and MiniOS
=================================

This package installs two commands:

* filin: AWDL link layer. It creates awdl0 and requires CAP_NET_ADMIN and
  CAP_NET_RAW for normal operation, plus a Wi-Fi adapter capable of monitor
  mode and frame injection.
* luftlift: AirDrop discovery, sender, and receiver.

Building from source
--------------------

The package supports amd64 and i386 and requires Rust/Cargo 1.85 or newer.
Debian patches adjust the dependency lock and source for Rust 1.85 and make
the chunked overflow test work on both architectures.

Rust dependencies are not bundled in Git or the Debian source package.
Cargo downloads the versions pinned by the patched Cargo.lock from crates.io
into debian/cargo-home. The build needs network access unless that cache has
already been populated. Builds in environments without network access must
populate the cache after applying the Debian patches, using cargo fetch --locked
with CARGO_HOME set to debian/cargo-home. The clean target removes this cache;
populate it after cleaning and retain it through the build.

Create the upstream orig tarball from the upstream Git commit, excluding
debian/. Do not reuse an orig tarball containing vendor/: dpkg-source retains
an existing orig tarball, even when debian/source/options excludes that directory.

Ubuntu 18.04 (Bionic) runtime compatibility
-------------------------------------------

The amd64 package can be built inside Bionic with a current Rust toolchain.
Such binaries link against Bionic glibc and require only libc6 >= 2.25, so they
run on the stock Bionic glibc 2.27.

Bionic's archive Rust/Cargo 1.65 is not sufficient to build the current
opendrop-rs dependency graph. Source builds therefore require Rust/Cargo 1.85
or newer. This is a build-toolchain limitation, not a runtime dependency.
